"Schematic of the residual-based intercept correction workflow on five synthetic observations. The fixed baseline predictor 2x is compared against observed targets y = 2x + 3 to yield residuals r = y - 2x. The mean residual across the five points determines the scalar correction b = 3, which is added to the baseline predictions to obtain corrected outputs 2x + b. In-sample evaluation on the same five observations confirms exact recovery with zero residual error."